{
  "chapter.681B4DB073FB10D5.title": "01 • MineColonies: A Living Colony",
  "task.3B7BB3BD7EFFB0B3.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.59C2E82B3B2557C7.title": "Start here: MineColonies",
  "quest.59C2E82B3B2557C7.quest_subtitle": "Start Here",
  "quest.59C2E82B3B2557C7.quest_desc": [
    "MineColonies turns a base into a working settlement. Citizens build blueprints, gather materials, cook, deliver supplies and research upgrades. You manage jobs and requests rather than placing every building block yourself. StyleColonies adds architectural choices to the build system.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/minecolonies.png width:330 height:150 align:center}",
    "",
    "&b&lChoose a branch&r",
    "• Foundations",
    "• People & Food",
    "• Supply & Research",
    "• Colony Projects",
    "",
    "Your route: site and supplies -> Town Hall and builder -> housing and food -> warehouse and couriers -> production, research and defense -> a self-supplied expansion.",
    "",
    "&eStart with the first equipment milestone, then follow the branch you need."
  ],
  "task.1798041B47F38631.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.55EDA03B1FB4A0D6.title": "Map legend & completion rules",
  "quest.55EDA03B1FB4A0D6.quest_subtitle": "Reference",
  "quest.55EDA03B1FB4A0D6.quest_desc": [
    "Follow a branch that solves your next problem. Equipment icons lead to concrete inventory milestones; the book card is a reference, and a large diamond marks a workshop project.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the setup before crafting. Item milestones detect your inventory without consuming items. Their practical checkmarks are optional reminders; final workshop projects require a practical confirmation. An item in your bag does not prove that a machine is configured. Existing equipment counts: do not rebuild a working system just for this map.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "JEI shows this pack's current recipes. Branches explain how the systems connect. Optional side projects are independent of the main route; no casino win is required."
  ],
  "task.40521F65525C7D15.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.40376CAADCA40739.title": "Choose land and a style",
  "quest.40376CAADCA40739.quest_subtitle": "Foundations",
  "quest.40376CAADCA40739.quest_desc": [
    "A colony needs room for future buildings, paths and changing elevations. A beautiful first house is less useful if every later blueprint overlaps a mountain.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Scout a broad area near materials. Preview the style you want with the Build Tool, including higher building levels, before committing. Plan a central storage area and leave walking space between entrances.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "StyleColonies supplies styles, not a second colony system. Large styles can require unusual decorative materials; inspect the preview and resource list first."
  ],
  "task.662ADB40F6532F72.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.71ADC4A26B994969.title": "A supply camp or ship",
  "quest.71ADC4A26B994969.quest_subtitle": "Foundations",
  "quest.71ADC4A26B994969.quest_desc": [
    "The supply structure gives you a starter shelter and colony equipment. It is a starting kit, not an operating colony.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Use a Supply Camp on suitable land, or choose the Supply Ship alternative in JEI. Resolve the highlighted placement obstructions, place the structure, and collect its Town Hall and Build Tool.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Choose either structure; this checklist accepts both routes. Do not place a second supply structure just for this guide."
  ],
  "task.072E1C7622F3D5F3.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.7BC3A2AC07F7B091.title": "Found your settlement",
  "quest.7BC3A2AC07F7B091.quest_subtitle": "Foundations",
  "quest.7BC3A2AC07F7B091.quest_desc": [
    "The Town Hall establishes the colony and gives access to citizen, work and permission management.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Place the Town Hall with the Build Tool at your planned center. Open it, establish/name the colony and inspect its information. Keep the area reachable by ordinary walking paths.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Placing a hut block and completing its building are different steps. Do not assume the blueprint has already been built."
  ],
  "task.2D3016661DBDBA7A.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.6DCD38F81AE6889F.title": "Your first builder",
  "quest.6DCD38F81AE6889F.quest_subtitle": "Foundations",
  "quest.6DCD38F81AE6889F.quest_desc": [
    "A builder constructs and upgrades the colony. Without one, a queue of hut blocks is only a queue of plans.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Place a Builder's Hut blueprint with the Build Tool. Assign an available citizen if necessary, request its construction, and open the hut to inspect the active job and required resources.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "WORK ORDER: Open the hut block, choose Build Options and request Build Building. A citizen must be assigned as the builder. The hut block alone is not a finished workplace: the citizen still has to place its schematic.",
    "",
    "FIRST JOB: Keep only one construction request active while learning. Put requested blocks in the builder inventory and provide the requested tool. When an item appears supplied but work is stopped, inspect the citizen interaction window for food, tool or path messages.",
    "",
    "UPGRADE RULE: A builder cannot construct arbitrary higher-level buildings. Improve the Builder's Hut when its level becomes the bottleneck. Preview the upgraded building footprint before building a road through it.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The builder can build their own initial hut. Queue one small project first so you learn the request system before expanding."
  ],
  "task.20A6328863326D41.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.5CE76239A3358618.title": "Read the request list",
  "quest.5CE76239A3358618.quest_subtitle": "Foundations",
  "quest.5CE76239A3358618.quest_desc": [
    "Most stalled jobs are a specific missing item, tool or condition. The Clipboard helps you see colony requests instead of guessing.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the builder's request, supply the exact requested material or a permitted substitution, then watch work resume. Use the hut resource interface and Clipboard to locate the next bottleneck.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A similar-looking block from another mod may not be accepted. The request tells you which item is needed."
  ],
  "task.789FE9B5023ED13F.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.61C01C6EB265C963.title": "Keep workers fed",
  "quest.61C01C6EB265C963.quest_subtitle": "People & Food",
  "quest.61C01C6EB265C963.quest_desc": [
    "Hungry citizens stop being productive. A Dining Hall distributes meals; the Chef's Kitchen is a separate production building.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build and staff a Dining Hall. Initially supply acceptable prepared food yourself and check that citizens can reach it and eat. Automate food production after this basic delivery loop works.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A worker with food problems needs food access, not another task in their queue. Check citizen status messages first."
  ],
  "task.310E33F64326FBFA.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.58F86761CC305FCA.title": "Housing and happiness",
  "quest.58F86761CC305FCA.quest_subtitle": "People & Food",
  "quest.58F86761CC305FCA.quest_desc": [
    "Residences provide stable housing and support population growth. More people require food, jobs and beds, not just recruitment.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build a Residence and inspect assignments. Check citizen happiness, access to shelter and basic needs before recruiting more workers.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Upgrade housing as your settlement grows. Avoid expanding population faster than your food supply and builders can support."
  ],
  "task.581D5E484F8DFBFC.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.082E6F2C61EF913B.title": "A reliable wood supply",
  "quest.082E6F2C61EF913B.quest_subtitle": "Supply & Research",
  "quest.082E6F2C61EF913B.quest_desc": [
    "Building consumes large amounts of wood. A Forester can turn an accessible planting area into a renewable supply.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build and staff the Forester's Hut. Supply the requested tool and saplings, check its work area, and confirm logs arrive in its inventory.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep decorative trees outside the selected work zone. Watch one full planting/harvesting cycle before depending on the output."
  ],
  "task.2B4CE46E6CBCAD74.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.2A3B0630147CC528.title": "Storage with a purpose",
  "quest.2A3B0630147CC528.quest_subtitle": "Supply & Research",
  "quest.2A3B0630147CC528.quest_desc": [
    "The Warehouse is the colony's shared store. It supports requests and crafting; an unrelated chest or RS disk is not automatically part of it.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build a Warehouse and stock it with common building materials. Inspect its racks and capacity, and keep access routes clear.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use colony-aware storage and delivery paths. Moving supplies into a warehouse is only half the system; couriers perform deliveries."
  ],
  "task.3A7962CE16538B8F.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.302E3FA9C8C56751.title": "Connect the supply chain",
  "quest.302E3FA9C8C56751.quest_subtitle": "Supply & Research",
  "quest.302E3FA9C8C56751.quest_desc": [
    "Couriers move requested supplies between the warehouse and workplaces, removing much of your manual delivery work.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build and staff a Courier's Hut. Trigger a small builder request using material already in the warehouse, then observe the courier delivering it.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "REQUEST TRACE: Builder asks for oak stairs -> Warehouse checks stock -> a trained Sawmill can craft missing stairs -> Courier moves inputs and the finished product. If the Sawmill does not know the recipe, adding more logs to storage will not solve the request.",
    "",
    "TEST: Stock 32 oak logs, teach the actual stair recipe used by your style, then queue a job that needs those stairs. Watch one delivery arrive. This is the point where your colony begins supplying construction rather than waiting for you at every step.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "If delivery stalls, check path access, courier availability, warehouse space and whether the exact item is stocked.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/minecolonies.png width:330 height:150 align:center}"
  ],
  "task.578044AF1711F7EF.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.41054430E156DC83.title": "Turn crops into meals",
  "quest.41054430E156DC83.quest_subtitle": "People & Food",
  "quest.41054430E156DC83.quest_desc": [
    "A Farm provides ingredients; a complete food chain also needs cooking and delivery.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build a Farm, configure its fields, provide seeds and tools, and observe a harvest. Route ingredients toward the relevant cooking workplace and keep meals available at the Dining Hall.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Do not empty every seed into a machine. Keep planting reserves and verify the crop type in the field setup."
  ],
  "task.405FAD816EBDC3DC.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.29940787C35F8C0A.title": "Teach the sawmill",
  "quest.29940787C35F8C0A.quest_subtitle": "Supply & Research",
  "quest.29940787C35F8C0A.quest_desc": [
    "A colony cannot fulfill a crafted-block request unless a suitable worker knows the recipe and has ingredients.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build and staff a Sawmill. Teach a simple supported wooden recipe, stock its inputs, and request that product through a building job.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Recipe capacity and available recipes depend on building level and research. Test one recipe before teaching an entire style palette."
  ],
  "task.5382EBCDBF41CBCA.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.0DEF901F188B8E8D.title": "Stone and tools",
  "quest.0DEF901F188B8E8D.quest_subtitle": "Supply & Research",
  "quest.0DEF901F188B8E8D.quest_desc": [
    "A Stonemason and later a Blacksmith help close the gap between raw resources and construction requests.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Add a Stonemason, teach a needed stone recipe and test it. Plan a Blacksmith for suitable tools and metal products as its research/build requirements become available.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Follow a request backward: final block -> crafter recipe -> ingredient supply -> courier. This reveals which link is actually missing."
  ],
  "task.311F5C88EA092A09.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.325942E4FB3ECE8D.title": "Research with a reason",
  "quest.325942E4FB3ECE8D.quest_subtitle": "Supply & Research",
  "quest.325942E4FB3ECE8D.quest_desc": [
    "Research unlocks buildings and improvements. Its prerequisites are part of colony progression, not a problem to bypass by crafting a hut early.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build a University when its requirements are met, assign a researcher, and select a research that solves a current need. Supply the requested materials and inspect the prerequisites and duration.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "PRIORITY: Open the research tree and select the unlock needed by your next production building. Read each node's building and material prerequisites before making its hut block. Research, a staffed finished hut and a taught recipe are three separate requirements.",
    "",
    "PLAN: Wood supply and food keep the settlement running; research should remove the next recurring shortage. A Sawmill saves repeated plank/stair crafting, while a Stonemason supports a stone-heavy style.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Choose a useful unlock before chasing every branch. Keep the colony loaded for work to progress under your pack's chunk-loading rules."
  ],
  "task.1FD8742FE8DE0365.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.43F029CD893A6FF1.title": "Upgrade your capacity",
  "quest.43F029CD893A6FF1.quest_subtitle": "Foundations",
  "quest.43F029CD893A6FF1.quest_desc": [
    "Upgrading the builder expands what they can construct. Higher-level workplaces also improve capabilities, storage and recipes.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the next upgrade's material list and builder-level requirement. Upgrade the Builder's Hut when needed, then upgrade one bottleneck workplace and verify the benefit.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Do not schedule every upgrade simultaneously. Preserve tools, food and access while your main builder is occupied."
  ],
  "task.419FB675F6DBA4A1.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3FCF38C8A5D69203.title": "Protect the workers",
  "quest.3FCF38C8A5D69203.quest_subtitle": "People & Food",
  "quest.3FCF38C8A5D69203.quest_desc": [
    "A larger colony needs guards and coverage near its workplaces. Walls alone do not equip or assign a guard.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build a Guard Tower, assign a guard, provide appropriate equipment and inspect patrol/guard settings. Light common paths and keep entrances usable by citizens.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Balance defense with food and production. Citizens' complaints and raid notifications are useful management signals."
  ],
  "task.2E018C6E27723ABD.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.055FBE8444D16357.title": "Recruit deliberately",
  "quest.055FBE8444D16357.quest_subtitle": "People & Food",
  "quest.055FBE8444D16357.quest_desc": [
    "Visitors and new citizens are useful only when you can give them a home, food and a productive role.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build a Tavern when ready. Inspect recruitment requirements and citizen skills, then choose a recruit suited to a real vacancy rather than filling every slot immediately.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Read the workplace's skill requirements. A suitable worker is more valuable than the first available name."
  ],
  "task.1D02F69698EF39CF.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.68E68A1EDDCDE2AC.title": "When a citizen stops",
  "quest.68E68A1EDDCDE2AC.quest_subtitle": "Colony Projects",
  "quest.68E68A1EDDCDE2AC.quest_desc": [
    "Idle animation is not a diagnosis. A citizen may need a tool, recipe, food, research, safe path or a finished building.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect the citizen's status, their hut, open requests and active work order in that order. Fix one cause, wait for the worker to react, and confirm the job advances.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Do not repeatedly break hut blocks to fix requests. Preserve their assignments and diagnose the missing condition instead."
  ],
  "task.757ABD17CEF8742D.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.1B6DFE41CB364491.title": "Project: supplied expansion",
  "quest.1B6DFE41CB364491.quest_subtitle": "Colony Projects",
  "quest.1B6DFE41CB364491.quest_desc": [
    "A functioning colony is a repeatable production and delivery system, not merely a collection of completed buildings.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Request one new building. Let your warehouse, couriers and crafters supply several of its materials. Resolve the remaining shortages, finish construction, staff it and explain its role in the colony.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use the same cycle for future expansion: identify a need, plan space, prepare materials, build, staff and verify."
  ],
  "task.065E60AEF153265E.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.2792DEA314B1D737.title": "The blueprint is the plan",
  "quest.2792DEA314B1D737.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Foundations",
  "quest.2792DEA314B1D737.quest_desc": [
    "The Build Tool selects style, rotation, position and level. The hut block is the management anchor of the finished structure; dropping it on the ground is not equivalent to selecting a blueprint.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Preview a Builder's Hut, rotate it so the entrance meets your future road, and inspect the higher-level footprint. Cancel the preview once, then place it deliberately. Keep this tool for every new colony building.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Reserve space for upgrades now. A later level can need a wider or taller footprint even when level 1 fits."
  ],
  "task.3C20201829CC9C3D.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.6240DEF3628AD483.title": "A full cycle of timber",
  "quest.6240DEF3628AD483.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Supply & Research",
  "quest.6240DEF3628AD483.quest_desc": [
    "A Forester is useful when it can cut, collect and replace trees while supplied with tools. A one-time harvest is not yet a renewable production loop.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Use an ordinary oak area for the first test. Supply the requested axe and saplings, observe cutting and replanting, then gather a 32-log sample. Add the courier route only after the worker can produce on their own.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "This inventory milestone records the sample, not who harvested it. Confirm the replanting behavior yourself before marking the practical task."
  ],
  "task.6CC26FB63CBA7023.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.0F19DC9B4E73CE79.title": "Logs become a building palette",
  "quest.0F19DC9B4E73CE79.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Supply & Research",
  "quest.0F19DC9B4E73CE79.quest_desc": [
    "Styles consume stairs, slabs, fences and doors as well as raw logs. Teaching the Sawmill the frequently requested products makes a small log supply much more useful.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Teach oak planks and oak stairs through supported recipes. Stock logs, allow an actual building request to trigger production, then collect a sample of the finished stairs. Return them to construction storage afterward.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Check the requested wood species. Oak stairs cannot satisfy a request for spruce stairs just because their shapes match."
  ],
  "task.02B5E48DE9AEC994.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.52B6CD346F8A754D.title": "Keep the tool supply running",
  "quest.52B6CD346F8A754D.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Supply & Research",
  "quest.52B6CD346F8A754D.quest_desc": [
    "Production eventually stops when workers wear out their tools. A Blacksmith turns tool replacement from a recurring personal errand into part of the colony supply chain.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Meet the visible research/building prerequisites, build and staff the hut, then teach one supported tool recipe requested by an existing worker. Stock the ingredients and follow one request to delivery.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use a tool grade the workplace can accept at its current level. More expensive is not automatically usable."
  ],
  "task.2E6348F250A7D9D9.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.4B56544D92EC807A.title": "Dinner before expansion",
  "quest.4B56544D92EC807A.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • People & Food",
  "quest.4B56544D92EC807A.quest_desc": [
    "A food reserve prevents a new construction project from consuming all your attention while citizens go hungry. Ingredients alone do not guarantee accessible meals.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build a reserve of 32 bread as a simple demonstration. Put acceptable food where your Dining Hall can use it, watch a citizen eat, and identify how the reserve will be replenished during the next build.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Bread is a demonstration item, not the only allowed food. Diversify meals according to the colony's actual needs."
  ],
  "task.3FCD96571384FCEE.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.15073C9BAA85201C.title": "Parallel construction, planned",
  "quest.15073C9BAA85201C.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Foundations",
  "quest.15073C9BAA85201C.quest_desc": [
    "A second Builder can reduce a construction queue, but it adds another demand stream for materials, tools and deliveries.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "After food and the warehouse route are reliable, prepare a second Builder's Hut in a different work area. Compare its workload and level with the first before assigning simultaneous upgrades.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "If both builders wait on the same missing recipe, more builders will not solve the bottleneck."
  ]
}
